FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       volScalarField;
    object      psi;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

dimensions      [0 1 0 0 0 0 0];

internalField   uniform 0;

// BOUNDARY DATA of the one-way translation (2026-09-29): zeroGradient on all four patches,
// as in every two-phase case of this repository. The exact solution is the signed distance
// of the translated circle, psi(x, t) = |x - c - U t| - R, with c = (0.25 0.5), U = (1 0 0),
// R = 0.15 (the implicitSphere and velocityModel blocks of system/fvSolution).
//
// Do NOT put the exact value on a patch here. MEASURED 2026-09-29 (a serial probe of four
// boundary variants at N = 64, 128, 256; STATUS 11.19): the SL fit reads every physical patch
// value as a stencil datum (SL_STENCIL_BOUNDARY_FACES include, the default), and
//   * the exact value on the OUTFLOW patch (right) made the SL update unstable at the outflow
//     edge at CFL 0.5: the edge error grew by a factor of about 1.1 per step and reached
//     4.5e5 at T at N = 256, with 96 false zero-set cells;
//   * the exact value on the INFLOW patch (left) made it unstable at CFL 1, where the
//     departure point of the first cell column lies outside the domain: E_GEOM_ALPHA_REL
//     1.79 at T at N = 128, with 2246 false zero-set cells in the inflow region.
// With zeroGradient on all four patches both runs are stable (outflow-edge error 1.7e-3 at
// N = 256, CFL 0.5; 8.8e-4 at N = 128, CFL 1).
//
// Consequence: the inflow region behind the circle (x < t) keeps psi0(0, y), which is at
// least 0.10 (no zero crossing), so the interface metrics are unaffected; the GLOBAL
// gradient metrics of this case measure that frozen region, not the transport. Use the
// band metrics.

boundaryField
{
    left
    {
        type            zeroGradient;
    }

    right
    {
        type            zeroGradient;
    }

    top
    {
        type            zeroGradient;
    }

    bottom
    {
        type            zeroGradient;
    }
}

